  "reason": "Evidence: The dominant finding is that scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l + multiprofile dramatically outperforms all scgpt-based configs (0.725 vs ~0.54). Within this family, transformer aggregation (config_027, 0.7250) beats avgpool (config_026, 0.7062) by ~2%, and weighted fusion has consistently outperformed concat in all prior comparisons (e.g., config_001 vs config_006). Question: config_048 tests the one remaining untested combination within our proven best architecture—scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l + transformer + concat—directly probing whether concat fusion might complement transformer aggregation differently than it does with avgpool. Why this is the best use of experiment 8: It is the lowest-risk, highest-information exploitation of our strongest result, testing the last untested variable in the top-performing family. Expected cost is moderate (~3.5–4 GPU hrs), comparable to config_027 (3.60 hrs) since the architecture is identical except for the fusion operation. Even if it does not surpass config_027, it definitively closes the fusion question for this architecture, allowing the final experiment to be directed at a more exploratory direction (e.g., singleprofile or an alternative image encoder) with full confidence about the current best."
}

